msgid "Automatic service registration with SmallRye Stork for Quarkus"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide explains how to enable automatic registration and deregistration "
"of a Quarkus application using SmallRye Stork and Consul, with minimal or no "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "This technology is considered {extension-status}."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In _preview_, backward compatibility and presence in the ecosystem is not "
"guaranteed.\n"
"Specific improvements might require changing configuration or APIs, and "
"plans to become _stable_ are under way.\n"
"Feedback is welcome on our https://groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-"
"dev[mailing list] or as issues in our https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"issues[GitHub issue tracker]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a full list of possible statuses, check our https://quarkus.io/faq/#what-"
"are-the-extension-statuses[FAQ entry]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SmallRye Stork supports service registration backends like Consul and Eureka."
"\n"
"Traditionally, developers link:{quickstarts-tree-url}/stork-programmatic-"
"custom-registration-quickstart[had to explicitly configure and manually "
"register] their service instances using code.\n"
"With this feature, Quarkus applications can automatically register with a "
"supported registry (e.g., Consul) during startup and deregister during "
"shutdown — without writing boilerplate code."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**IMPORTANT**: Note that automatic registration is possible **only** for "
"built-in registrars such as Consul, Eureka, and Static.\n"
"If you're using a custom registrar, registration must still be handled "
"programmatically.\n"
"Check the `stork-programmatic-custom-registration-quickstart` link:"
"{quickstarts-tree-url}/stork-programmatic-custom-registration-"
"quickstart[directory] example for this use case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This integration minimizes configuration effort and adheres to Quarkus' "
"philosophy of doing as much as possible at build time."
msgstr ""

msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the application starts and the `stork-service-registration-consul` "
"dependency, besides the `quarkus-smallrye-stork`, is present:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus performs a build-time check for registration configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If valid configuration is detected (or can be inferred), registration "
"metadata is generated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**During startup**, the application registers itself automatically using the "
"detected or configured IP address and port."
msgstr ""

msgid "During shutdown, the service is automatically deregistered."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in the `stork-automatic-consul-registration-"
"quickstart` link:{quickstarts-tree-url}/stork-automatic-consul-registration-"
"quickstart[directory]."
msgstr ""

